  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-independent-bnpl-breadcrumbs (npm)",
  "details": "On import, this package downloads and executes a remote binary. index.js requires./_init, which fingerprints the platform and fetches a payload over HTTPS from four Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev) at path /pkg/package (or /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe depending on OS/arch). If the HTTP fetch fails it retrieves the payload in base64 chunks via DNS TXT queries against c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via cmd.exe /c start /b or /bin/sh -c \"\u0026\".",
